# What the published package carries: dist/src/ (the compiled node, credential
# and icon), package.json, LICENSE and README.md. Nothing else.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THIS FILE.
#
# package.json declares a `files` allowlist, and when that field is present npm
# builds the tarball from it and does NOT apply this root `.npmignore`. Measured
# on npm 12.0.1: with `"files": ["dist", ...]` and a `dist/test/` rule here, the
# compiled test tree shipped anyway — twelve files and 90 kB of test code, in an
# artefact whose whole point is that an auditor can read all of it. The gate
# `npm run lint:package` caught it, because it inspects the packed artefact and
# not this file.
#
# So the allowlist is the mechanism that decides, and it is written narrowly:
# `dist/src` rather than `dist`. This file is kept as a second line for the case
# where `files` is ever removed from the manifest — it is NOT load-bearing today,
# and no rule may be added here on the assumption that it will be enforced.

# Sources, tests and gates never ship: what n8n installs is the compiled
# artefact, and the analyser audits that artefact and not this repository.
src/
test/
scripts/
docs/

# The compiled tests do not ship either. `files` is what actually keeps them
# out; see the note above.
dist/test/

# Tooling and repository furniture.
tsconfig.json
.editorconfig
.github/
.gitignore
*.tgz
*.log
.DS_Store
